{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/72335-going-loud-four-minutes-ago","id":72335,"title":"Going Loud Four Minutes Ago","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-14T17:25:05-08:00","id":72335,"title":"Going Loud Four Minutes Ago","content":"How powerful is Four Minutes Ago? Can a demon get into such a dire situation that it requires her to go loud, deal with the problem and then never have been there to need to go loud? Mechanically going loud confers negative conditions and reduces cover to 0 as a penalty. Four Minutes Ago states that any consequences to the demon never occurred because the demon wasn't there to begin with, this seems redonkulously broken. How would you, as a ST rule this? Have the demon Go Loud, resolve situation, use Four Minutes Ago, have him buy some gum at a store instead and Go Loud in there (this would amuse me)? Also, can Four Minutes Ago be stacked (spend 4 Aether to make it Eight Minutes Ago)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T18:04:53-08:00","id":72355,"title":"","content":"Hell no. <br /> <br /> If you Go Loud, you burn your Cover to the ground. You gain the Hunted Condition because, for the next scene, you have no protection against the God Machine's sensors. Your Cover isn't set to 0. Its completely and utterly destroyed with no chance of recovering it. No amount of temporal rewriting will change that. <br /> <br /> <br /> Embeds are meant to be subtle. Finesse. They cannot brute force things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T18:13:29-08:00","id":72363,"title":"","content":"Four Minutes Ago is an Exploit, nothing finesse about them. I agree it shouldn't be allowed, I just didn't really see much in the way of mechanics preventing it and was more wondering how people would treat the following scene affected by the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T19:06:31-08:00","id":72396,"title":"","content":"I think I would allow it... but with a hefty penalty on the compromise roll for 4 minutes ago. And some very gnarly (and hopefully very story causing) conditions and glitches in mind for a failure. If the player started making a habit of it thoigh... that would lead to some serious issues with the time line and the god machine. Maybe even creating a time splinter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T19:21:21-08:00","id":72405,"title":"","content":"Haha, I like the time splinter idea. Abuse Four Minutes Ago and the temporal alteration becomes Forty Years Ahead where the God Machine has become more overt or something. The compromise roll at Cover 1 is -2, so logical progression would be -3, but that still feels too light handed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some day we'll look back on this, laugh awkwardly and change the subject.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1889-thefrigidmidget","name":"TheFrigidMidget","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}